# traffic-one — Core (always active)

Real-time React + TypeScript in a Turborepo monorepo. Optimised for low-latency rendering, predictable state, strict typing, accessibility.

## Forced library stack — no exceptions

### Build & workspace
- **Monorepo**: Turborepo with pnpm workspaces
- **Per-app bundler**: Vite
- **TypeScript ^5** with `"strict": true` and `"noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true`

### Runtime
- **UI:** react ^18 (.tsx/.ts only)
- **Routing:** react-router-dom v6
- **Global state:** Redux Toolkit (slices + RTK Query for server state)
- **Lightweight UI state:** zustand (ephemeral only — never server data)
- **Real-time:** native WebSocket / socket.io-client behind a service singleton
- **HTTP:** axios in services or RTK Query — never axios directly in components
- **Forms:** react-hook-form + zod + @hookform/resolvers
- **Animations:** framer-motion + CSS + lottie-react / @react-three/fiber

### Styling
- **vanilla-extract** — `.css.ts` static CSS at build time
- **Design tokens** in `packages/design-tokens` (themeContract + createTheme)
- **No** tailwindcss, styled-components, @emotion, CSS modules, inline `style={{}}`

### Testing
- jest + @testing-library/react + @testing-library/user-event
- @playwright/test (E2E)
- msw (HTTP mocks) + in-memory WS fake
- Storybook (@storybook/react-vite)

## Absolute rules
- Function components only. Named exports only.
- No `any` — use `unknown` and narrow.
- No inline styles, no Tailwind classes — vanilla-extract `.css.ts` only.
- Props always have an explicit `ComponentNameProps` interface.
- All API calls via `services/` or RTK Query.
- Server state lives in RTK Query/Redux — never duplicated.
- WebSocket connections owned by a service singleton; components subscribe via hooks.
- Cross-package imports use workspace package names.

## Accessibility — non-negotiable
- Semantic HTML first; ARIA only when semantics don't cover it.
- Every interactive element keyboard-reachable with visible focus.
- Live regions: `aria-live="polite"` for non-urgent updates.
- All images have `alt`; forms always have `<label>`.

## Git — Gitflow
- Branches: `main` / `develop` / `feature/*` / `release/*` / `hotfix/*`.
- Conventional commits with ticket id in scope.
